{title: Like a Tree by the Water}
{subtitle: Psalm 1}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Blessed is the one who does not [Eb]walk in the counsel of the wic[Bb]ked
Who does not [Eb]stand in the way of sinners [Bb]
Who does not [Eb]sit in the seat of mockers [Gm]
But whose de[Eb]light is in the instruction of the [F]LORD
And [Eb]who murmurs over his instruction day and [F]night
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]He is like [F]a tree [Gm]transplanted be[Eb]side channels of wa[Bb]ter
Yielding [F]its fruit in [Gm]season, its [Eb]leaf never withering
[Bb]In all that he [F]does, he [Gm]thrives
[Eb]Like a tree transplanted [F]beside channels of water
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Not so the wic[Bb]ked
They are [Eb]like chaff that the wind blows a[Bb]way
Therefore the [Eb]wicked will not stand in the judg[Gm]ment
[Eb]Nor sinners in the assembly of the right[F]eous
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]He is like [F]a tree [Gm]transplanted be[Eb]side channels of water
[Bb]Yielding [F]its fruit in [Gm]season, its [Eb]leaf never withering
[Bb]In all that he [F]does, he [Gm]thrives
[Eb]Like a tree transplanted [F]beside channels of water
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | ×2
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [F] | [F] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
For [Gm]the LORD knows the way of the [Eb]righteous
But [Bb]the way of the wicked [F]will perish
[Eb]The LORD knows [F]the way of the righteous
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
